{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"why","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class","level":2,"anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" generates that class for you (","type":"text"},{"code":"<StructName>Observer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and wires up the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers take ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". They never ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", never ","type":"text"},{"code":"throw","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and never call I\/O directly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through ","type":"text"},{"code":"send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs effects in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" so they don’t block UI. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible","text":"4. Persistence is invisible","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers mutate "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" properties; "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" records every change in a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" debounces and drains those changesets through "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" closures.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You never write ","type":"text"},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point","text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two structural patterns:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core middleware"}]},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","isActive":true},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"text":" for undo; ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"text":" keypaths for persistence).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain plugins"}]},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The decision rule: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"does this need to know your action type?"}]},{"type":"text","text":" If no, write core middleware and use "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State","text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Form inputs read from the store and dispatch on write. Use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the common case (read one property, dispatch one action), and fall back to "},{"code":"Binding(get:set:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the read is a transformation (optional unwraps, derived values) or the setter wraps the dispatch in animation or branching. Don’t buffer mutable form state in "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and write back on a button."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", those plugins are blind to it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries","text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" snapshots in "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it must run "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" drains changelogs in "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The recommended order:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose","text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is built for "},{"code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation ("},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"@concurrent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with "},{"code":"async\/await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not","text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux gives you a "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppEnvironment"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A network layer (use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"text":" and Swidux doesn’t care).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Anti-patterns","text":"Anti-patterns","type":"heading","level":2},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try"},{"text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Calling ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"text":" from inside a reducer — use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Owning the store with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@StateObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — use ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObservableObject"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Buffering form state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Registering "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" before "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" — snapshot must precede mutation."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Explanation","title":"Explanation"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Design Principles","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","title":"Send","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Send"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","role":"article","title":"Architecture & Performance","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","title":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Swidux","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","title":"StateWriter","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp","title":"Build Your First Swidux App","kind":"article","type":"topic","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","title":"Plugin Architecture","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/binding(_:sending:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","role":"symbol","conformance":{"constraints":[{"code":"State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"title":"binding(_:sending:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/binding(_:sending:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"binding"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"KeyPath","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7KeyPathC"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"State"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Observer","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux0A10ObservableP8ObserverQa"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sending","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Action"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Binding","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"type":"text","text":" that reads a property through the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"observer tree and dispatches an action when written.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","title":"SwiduxPlugin","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","title":"ChangeSet","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","title":"Effect","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Effect"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"role":"symbol","title":"UndoPlugin","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndoPlugin"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","title":"EntityStore","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}]}}}